-- title:
--   Parametric Tarski–Seidenberg theorem (Łojasiewicz's version) for one eliminated variable
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal A$ be a subring of the ring of real-valued functions on a set $E$, and let $\mathcal F$ be any family of subsets of $E$ that contains $\{a : f(a) > 0\}$ for every $f \in \mathcal A$ and is stable under complement and finite intersection (so $\mathcal F \supseteq S(\mathcal A)$). Let $f_1,\dots,f_s \in \mathcal A[t]$ be polynomials in one variable $t$ with coefficients in $\mathcal A$, and $\nu_1,\dots,\nu_s \in \{-1,0,1\}$. Then
--
--   $$\{\, a \in E \;:\; \exists\, t \in \mathbb R,\ \operatorname{sign} f_i(a,t) = \nu_i \ (i = 1,\dots,s) \,\} \in \mathcal F,$$
--
--   where $f_i(a,t)$ is $f_i$ with every coefficient evaluated at $a$.
--
--   Role: this is the parametric Tarski-Seidenberg theorem used in the proof of Gabrielov's theorem of the complement (the parent): eliminating one real variable from sign conditions whose coefficients are analytic functions of the parameters keeps the set in the Boolean algebra generated by those functions.
--
--   **Formalization Note**: $S(\mathcal A)$ is expressed impredicatively: the projection lies in every family $\mathcal F$ with the closure properties above, which is equivalent to lying in the smallest such family $S(\mathcal A)$. The statement is the case $k = 1$ of BM88 Theorem 2.2 for a set described by one sign condition; general sets of $S(\mathcal A[t])$ are finite unions of these.
-- source:
--   E. Bierstone, P. D. Milman, Semianalytic and subanalytic sets, Publ. Math. IHES 67 (1988) 5-42, https://www.numdam.org/item/10.1007/BF02699126.pdf, Theorem 2.2 (Lojasiewicz's version of the Tarski-Seidenberg theorem) with the definition of S(A) at the start of Section 2, p. 10

import Mathlib

namespace NonsmoothLojasiewicz.Continuous

theorem tarski_seidenberg_parametric {A : Type*} (R : Subring (A → ℝ)) {κ : Type} (F : Finset κ)
    (ev : κ → Polynomial R) (ν : κ → SignType) (Fam : Set (Set A))
    (hpos : ∀ f ∈ R, {a | 0 < f a} ∈ Fam) (hcompl : ∀ S ∈ Fam, Sᶜ ∈ Fam)
    (hinter : ∀ S ∈ Fam, ∀ T ∈ Fam, S ∩ T ∈ Fam) :
    {a : A | ∃ x : ℝ, ∀ i ∈ F, SignType.sign
      (((ev i).map ((Pi.evalRingHom (fun _ : A => ℝ) a).comp R.subtype)).eval x) = ν i} ∈ Fam := by sorry

end NonsmoothLojasiewicz.Continuous
